# K7 capture and frame formats (normative)

## 1. Pack container (`base.k7`)

- Magic: `K7PK` (4 bytes)
- Entry count: `uint32` big-endian
- Repeated entries: `name_len uint32`, `name bytes`, `blob_len uint32`, `frame blob`

Held-out padded lane: `/app/environment/bundle/k7/var089.pad` (filler suffix must not change canonical stamp when logical frame unchanged).

## 2. Frame blob (`K7FR`)

- Magic: `K7FR` (4 bytes)
- Body length: `uint32` big-endian
- TLV body: sequence of `{tag u8, len u16 BE, value bytes}`

Tags (see module constants): filler `0x00`, alternate `0x10` / `0x11`, usage `0x20`, nest `0x80`.

## 3. Reference instrument

`/opt/k7probe/dy observe --chunk PATH` returns JSON:

```json
{"canon_hex": "<lowercase hex>", "body_len": <int>}
```

Partition invariance: delivering the same frame bytes in one read or split reads must yield identical `canon_hex`.

## 4. Public sanity command

`/app/environment/tools/check-k7.sh` exercises bundled pack bytes without replacing the instrument.
